{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shore\nA land of mystic charm and beauty to adore\nFourteen days shall be the length of thy sojourn there\nWith each day a new wonder waiting to be shared\n\nDay One\nThou shalt arrive in Tokyo's bustling streets\nWhere neon lights do dance and ancient traditions meet\nCheck into thy hotel and take a moment to rest\nThen forth to explore the city's vibrant best\n\nVisit Shibuya Crossing where fashion doth reign\nAnd in Harajuku's streets discover youthful fancies' domain\nAt night take in a sumo match or a Kabuki play\nTo experience Japan's rich cultural heritage in all its sway\n\nDay Two\nRise early and head to Tsukiji's famous fish market\nWhere fresh sushi doth await thy eager taste\nThence to the Meiji Shrine a tranquil oasis in the heart\nOf bustling Tokyo where peace and calm doth never depart\n\nDay Three\nTake a day trip to Nikko a city of grandeur and might\nWhere temples and shrines do stand in all their ancient light\nThe Toshogu Shrine a UNESCO World Heritage site\nDoth await thy visit with its ornate and colorful sight\n\nDay Four\nReturn to Tokyo and visit the Tokyo Tower's lofty height\nFrom whence thou shalt behold the city's sprawling sight\nIn the evening stroll through the Imperial Palace East Garden\nWhere cherry blossoms bloom in beauty and in gentle surrender\n\nDay Five\nTravel to Kyoto a city of ancient charm and beauty rare\nWhere temples and gardens do abound and historic tales do share\nVisit the Fushimi Inari Shrine a veritable wonder to behold\nWith its thousands of vermilion torii gates that do stretch and unfold\n\nDay Six\nIn Kyoto visit the Kinkaku-ji Temple a sight most fair\nA golden pavilion that doth shimmer in the morning air\nThence to the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove a tranquil and peaceful place\nWhere nature's beauty doth entwine with a sense of mystic space\n\nDay Seven\nVisit the Nijo Castle a UNESCO World Heritage site\nWhere the nightingale floors do creak beneath thy feet so light\nThence to the Kiyomizu-dera Temple a wooden stage most high\nWhere the city of Kyoto doth unfold in a panoramic sigh\n\nDay Eight\nTake a day trip to the Nara a city of ancient might\nWhere temples and shrines do stand in all their historic light\nVisit the Todai-ji Temple a UNESCO World Heritage site\nWhere the Great Buddha doth sit in all his golden might\n\nDay Nine\nReturn to Kyoto and visit the Gion District a place of old\nWhere geishas do stroll and traditional arts do unfold\nIn the evening take in a traditional Kyoto-style dinner\nWhere local delicacies do await thy eager taste and pleasure\n\nDay Ten\nTravel to Hiroshima a city of peace and of sorrow's sway\nWhere the Hiroshima Peace Memorial Park doth stand in all its gray\nVisit the Hiroshima Castle a historic site of old\nWhere the city's history doth unfold in a tale of sorrow told\n\nDay Eleven\nVisit the Miyajima Island a place of natural beauty rare\nWhere the Itsukushima Shrine doth seem to float on the air\nThence to the Hiroshima Museum of Art a place of cultural might\nWhere local art and history doth unfold in all its light\n\nDay Twelve\nReturn to Tokyo and spend the day at leisure\nExploring the city's many wonders and hidden treasures to discover\nVisit the Akihabara District a place of electronic delight\nWhere gadgets and gizmos do abound in all their colorful light\n\nDay Thirteen\nVisit the Hamarikyu Gardens a tranquil oasis in the heart\nOf bustling Tokyo where peace and calm doth never depart\nThence to the Meiji Shrine a peaceful and serene place\nWhere the city's stress doth melt away in a gentle space\n\nDay Fourteen\nThy journey to Japan doth come to an end at last\nA journey of wonder and discovery that doth forever last\nFare thee well Japan a land of mystic charm and beauty rare\nMay thy memories of this journey forever be a treasure to share", "logprobs": [